  "text": "Surgery | Animal Specialty Center\nSkip to Primary Content\nBook\nContact Us\nMap\n9 Odell Plaza,\nYonkers,\nNY,\n10701\nCall\n(914) 457-4000\nEmergency\nEmergency\nPhone:\n(914) 457-4000\nAddress:\n9 Odell Plaza,\nYonkers,\nNY,\n10701\nOur Team\nServices\nCardiology\nDermatology\nEmergency\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nRadiation Oncology\nSurgery\nPet Owners\nReferring Veterinarians\nCareer Growth\nEmergency\nContact Us\nIf you’ve been referred to our hospital or would like to schedule a consultation with one of our surgeons, please call us to make an appointment.\nSurgery\nSurgery\nOur compassionate surgical team is dedicated to supporting you and your pet every step of the way. When your pet requires advanced surgery, it’s important to know that our surgeons have undergone years of additional training beyond veterinary school to become specialists. They have used their expertise to help hundreds of pets and have access to state-of-the-art equipment to perform a wide range of advanced procedures.\nHere at Animal Specialty Center, we offer a full range of surgical services, including (but not limited to):\nSoft-Tissue Surgery\nGastrointestinal Surgery\nCardiovascular Surgery\nAirway Surgery\nThoracic Surgery\nUrogenital surgery\nLiver and Gallbladder Surgery\nAbdominal Surgery\nOncologic (cancer and tumor) Surgery\nSkin Grafts and Reconstructive Surgery\nAmputations\nHead and Neck Surgery\nHernia Repair\nOrthopedic Surgery\nTibial Plateau Leveling Osteotomy (TPLO) for cranial cruciate ligament injuries\nPatellar Luxation Correction\nFracture Repair\nAngular Limb Deformity (ALD) Correction\nMinimally Invasive Procedures:\nThese techniques keep your pet more comfortable than some traditional approaches, and often lead to a quicker recovery with less pain.\nArthroscopy for conditions involving joints\nThoracoscopy for conditions within the chest cavity\nLaparoscopy for conditions within the abdominal cavity\nReasons for Veterinary Surgery\nVeterinary surgery is often used in conjunction with internal medicine, medical oncology, radiation oncology, physical rehabilitation, and neurology. While not all health issues require surgery, it can be the best option for certain conditions. Common reasons your pet might need surgery include:\nBlockages: Foreign objects ingested by your pet can lead to blockages that require surgical removal.\nCancer: Surgery may be necessary to remove tumors or masses, often as part of a broader treatment plan.\nInjuries: Severe injuries, such as broken bones or major wounds, may need surgical intervention for proper repair.\nOrthopedic Issues: Conditions like fractures or severe arthritis can benefit from specialized orthopedic procedures.\nAt Animal Specialty Center, we offer a comprehensive range of surgical services to address these and other needs.\nAnimal Specialty Center\n9 Odell Plaza\nYonkers\n,\nNY\n10701\nT:\n(914) 457-4000\nF:\n(914) 457-4001\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nContact Us\nOur Team\nCareer Growth\nPet Owners\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nCookie Preferences\nDo Not Sell or Share My Information\n©\nCopyright\n2026",
